				 Census 






			 If you have not received your census or are new to City, you may print a copy of this year's census below and return it to the address indicated on the form. Print the  form , sign, and return.  Click here for a blank census form . 

 You’ve received your census - what’s next ? 


	 Review Census sheet information and reply within 10 days of receipt. 

		 If the information is correct, sign and return 
		 If the information isn’t correct, make the corrections, sign and return 




 What happens if I don’t reply to the first mailing?   

 The Commission will send out a postcard to voters who haven’t replied. If you do not reply to this second mailing, your voter registration status will be changed to inactive. You are still on the voter rolls, and are still eligible to vote, however, on election day, you will be required to sign an affirmation and show ID to vote.   

 How can you return your census? 


	 Outside Medford City Hall in the red, white, and blue drop box 
